WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.989 --> 00:00:07.379
Science is a slow process and it’s yet to
answer many of the great questions about life,

00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:09.700
death, time, space etc.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.839
But some people are rather impatient and would
rather make up their own mystical answers

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:17.360
to life's great mysteries.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.689
People often turn to theology, philosophy
and the occult, to try and find answers of

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.099
their own.&nbsp;

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:28.789
Mysticism is the search for apparent hidden
truths through a range of special techniques

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:34.610
such as meditation, rituals, spiritual development,
certain drugs, or by just wearing a second

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.560
hand kimono and quoting David Bowie lyrics.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:43.200
So today we look at the dark and rather fearsome
never-world of mysticism and discover some

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.620
of the most influential mystics in history.&nbsp;

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:56.710
Aleister Crowley was an occultist, a painter,
a novelist, a mountaineer, a poet, and possibly

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.610
a spy for Great Britain.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:02.500
The press, of the late nineteen-hundreds,
were not very fond of Crowley and dubbed him

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.880
“The Wickedest Man in the World” since
they said he was a Satanist.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.960
He founded the religion of Thelema and wrote
The Book of Law, which contains its guidelines.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:18.009
He wrote it in 1904 in Cairo, during his honeymoon,
which I’m sure his wife, Rose, was delighted

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:19.009
about.

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:22.780
The main concept of Thelema is “Do what
thou wilt".

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:27.790
Crowley had previously been a member of the
famous occult society The Golden Dawn but

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:32.869
they were not fans of his bisexuality and
lifestyle so he left after about a year, losing

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:37.290
out on his Egyptian clothing discount card
and subscription to Spooky Tales monthly.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:42.020
It’s thought that his membership could have
been an intelligence operation to undermine

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:45.340
Samuel Liddell Mathers, one of Golden Dawn’s
founders.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:50.350
There are many other events in Crowley’s
life that could have been undercover work,

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.429
such as when he wrote German propaganda during
WW1.

00:01:53.429 --> 00:01:59.549
Our next mystic rose all the way from the
peasant villages of Siberia to the top of

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:02.119
the court of Tsar Nicholas II.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:07.959
Grigori Rasputin left behind his wife and
three remaining children in his early twenties

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:12.030
to become a monk, claiming he’d had a vison
from Our Lady of Kazan.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:17.640
By 30, he had become a religious wanderer,
walking between holy places and receiving

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.580
hospitality in exchange for religious wisdom
and likes on Instagram.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:27.610
Through his unique interpretations of the
scriptures, and his hypnotic steely gaze,

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:32.960
he quickly built a following and ended up
in St Petersburg around 1904, where he was

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.420
eventually introduced to the Tsar.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:40.090
He cemented his place with the royal family
through his mystical healing powers.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.740
He supposedly helped the Tsar’s son, Alexei,
recover from near death through the power

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:51.160
of prayer but it’s probably down to the
fact that he stopped him taking aspirin, which

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.170
was having a savage effect on the boy’s
haemophilia.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.760
He became a trusted advisor to the royals
and even helped them to take major military

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:04.380
decisions during WW1, encouraging them to
withdraw large numbers of troops, either to

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:10.050
reduce casualties or perhaps to free up German
troops to move westwards and defeat the British.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:14.480
We weren't this crazy monk’s biggest fans
and it’s been rumoured British Intelligence

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.510
had a hand in his mysterious death.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:22.060
It could have just been the work of the Russian
aristocracy though, since they were not fond

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:27.140
of Rasputin either, thanks to his influence
and his slow descent into debauchery, given

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.040
that he grew a love of dessert wines and brothels.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:36.120
His body was found floating in the river and
it’s alleged that he was poisoned with cyanide,

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:39.620
shot in the kidney and head and then drowned.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.330
If you’re going to murder someone, you may
as well do it right.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:48.230
Another Russian now, born some forty years
before Rasputin in 1831.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:54.210
Helena Blavatsky was a spirit medium who co-founded
the Theosophical Society.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:04:00.690
Theosophy is the idea that you can find salvation
through discovering the mysteries of the universe,

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.340
presumably by being really really good at
googling.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:09.250
The aim of the group was to follow The Intelligent
Evolution of All Existence, something which

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.740
our modern world has definitely fought hard
against, just take a look around.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:18.209
Helena claimed to have gathered various ancient
wisdom and psychic powers from her travels

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:23.759
around the world starting in 1849, from the
Americas to India and Tibet.

00:04:23.759 --> 00:04:28.069
Her biographers suspect that this was a lie
and she was actually just in Europe, photoshopping

00:04:28.069 --> 00:04:32.280
the Himalayas into her selfies while she was
really sitting in a Starbucks somewhere in

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.280
Poland.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.799
Hey we’ve all done it, Helena.

00:04:34.799 --> 00:04:39.879
She did become hugely famous for her occult
teachings and although now her name is less

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:44.939
well known, in those times it was recognised
internationally, as much as any modern trend

00:04:44.939 --> 00:04:46.629
setting guru.

00:04:46.629 --> 00:04:51.310
She was basically the Kim Kardashian of the
occult, with a smaller bottom.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.210
A more modern mystic now.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:59.800
Nirmala Srivastava, who died in 2011, was
the founder of Sahaja Yoga, a practice that

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.060
covers a bit more than tight leggings and
being able to suck your own toes.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:09.389
It’s all about reaching a state of awareness
and unlocking your Kundalini.

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:13.949
Kundalini is said to be a body energy that
flows through your various Chakras, which

00:05:13.949 --> 00:05:17.669
are like invisible USB ports that run down
the centre of your being.

00:05:17.669 --> 00:05:22.139
This is why you should never drop a yoga teacher
in a bath, they may electrocute themselves.

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:27.950
The general aim is to reach thoughtless awareness,
where you understand everything but you’re

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:32.300
not really paying attention, a bit like when
you keep eating peanuts even though you’re

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.819
not really hungry.

00:05:33.819 --> 00:05:40.610
She claimed in 1979 to be the embodiment of
Shakti, the Hindu idea of cosmic energy that

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.070
runs throughout the universe.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:47.650
She’s also named herself the Maitreya, from
Buddhism, and Mahdi, of Islam.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:51.469
She also claimed the Iron Throne and said
she knew what was in the suitcase in Pulp

00:05:51.469 --> 00:05:52.469
Fiction.

00:05:52.469 --> 00:05:57.879
And finally, a woman with an astonishing life,
who helped lead the American suffrage movement

00:05:57.879 --> 00:06:01.630
and was the first ever female to run for president.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:08.050
Victoria Woodhull was born in rural Ohio to
an illiterate mother and a con-man father.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:12.449
She was a bright child at school but could
not attend often and had to leave very young

00:06:12.449 --> 00:06:16.990
when her father burnt their mill down in a
shady insurance scam.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:23.469
She then became a magnetic healer, by following
the work of Austrian mystic Franz Mesmer,

00:06:23.469 --> 00:06:27.400
and probably a good dash of her old man’s
con man skills.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.199
But she quickly moved on to greater things.

00:06:30.199 --> 00:06:35.259
While still supporting the spiritualist movement,
her and her sister became the first women

00:06:35.259 --> 00:06:40.150
to open a stock broking firm when they set
up on Wall St in 1870.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:44.419
Within a few successful months, they used
the money they had raised to launch a newspaper,

00:06:44.419 --> 00:06:48.069
primarily as a tool to back Victoria’s presidential
campaign.

00:06:48.069 --> 00:06:53.430
The paper focussed on feminist issues, supporting
ideas such as free love, vegetarianism, sex

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.350
education and legalised prostitution.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:00.659
It was like Vogue, if you swapped all the
adverts for actual content.

00:07:00.659 --> 00:07:06.000
When the 1872 presidential vote came around,
Victoria was actually in prison, since she

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.000
had ruffled some feathers by devoting a full
paper issue to the affair between Elizabeth

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:17.080
Tilton and Reverend Henry Ward Beecher, a
prominent Protestant minister in New York,

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.800
highlighting the hypocrisy of the sexual double
standard between men and woman, that had led

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.360
her to believe in free love.&nbsp;

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:28.600
We would all like to find the hidden secrets
of the universe and unlock some kind of secret

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:33.789
path to happiness and enlightenment, but if
you want to become a mystic you first need

00:07:33.789 --> 00:07:36.309
to get a really cool sounding name.

00:07:36.309 --> 00:07:41.219
I mean just look at the people we’ve talked
about today, Crowley, Rasputin, Blavatsky,

00:07:41.219 --> 00:07:42.219
Srivastava.

00:07:42.219 --> 00:07:48.960
Obviously, as it seems, one needs a sufficiently
awesome name to be able to align one’s chakras,

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.919
reach a higher level of being and heal the
sick.

00:07:51.919 --> 00:08:14.369
I’m afraid if you’re going to call yourself
“Steve the mystic” you’re not going

00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:18.729
to be so mystical now are you?

